; Tagged types (`#6.n(...)`).
; - A bare top-level `tagged = #6.42(text)` is a single-type tag wrapper of a primitive; it emits a
;   transparent `pub type Tagged = String` that DROPS the tag from the standalone API. That
;   transparent-alias behavior is deliberately pinned pending a maintainer decision (see
;   TESTING_ROADMAP "Pending decisions": auto-wrap vs opt-in).
; - `tagged_newtype = #6.42(text) ; @newtype` opts into the tag-writing wrapper via the comment DSL.
;   The trailing directive is threaded through the single-type unwrap in `parse_type` rather than
;   silently lost, so this emits a real newtype whose serialize writes tag 42 and whose deserialize
;   rejects a wrong tag. (`holder` references it so the embed role compiles.)
tagged = #6.42(text)
tagged_newtype = #6.42(text) ; @newtype
holder = [payload: tagged_newtype]
